// The port's own text (#189, ADR 0108): MT_TEXT(id, "English"). The id is the key in a text
// pack's Port.strings; "{0}", "{1}", ... are places a text fills in (tr(id, {args})), which a
// translation keeps. The English is what the overlays drew before the table, byte for byte.
// The settings registry's labels and help and the settings menu's action rows are not here:
// their English stays in their rows, keyed "setting.<key>.label" / ".help" and
// "action.<key>.label" / ".help" / ".button" / ".confirm" (tr_key). No include guard: the
// includer defines MT_TEXT.

